Z||000000||jlhuber||03-18-2001||03:34 PM||||Has anyone thought of swapping a 2.0L turbo from a late 80's early 90's Grand Am into a Fiero?  Here is the thread that sparked the idea into my head  <A HREF="http://www.syty.net/ubb/Forum1/HTML/000383.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.syty.net/ubb/Forum1/HTML/000383.html</A>   Being that it came from a Pontiac, I would think that it would swap in quite easily.  Anyone have performance numbers for this engine?  It may have potential to be an easy, low buck swap for the 2.5s'.<P>the post by "warmpancakes" after the turbo barstool is the only reference that gives me the idea.<BR>------------------<BR>--Jess--<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/blackeye2/double0smile.gif">    <BR>If you expect the unexpected, was it really even unexpected in the first place?<p>[This message has been edited by jlhuber (edited 03-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Formula 18||03-18-2001||04:33 PM||||Can it be done?-- Yes<BR>Has it been done?-- Yes<BR>Could you buy one new with this engine in 88?-Yes<P>I even have an article comparing it to a SD4 and a Miller-Woods 2.8<P>I can try and send it to you if you want. <P>I have thought i minght be a good swap too I found a Turbo J-car and a Fiero w/ a bad 2.5 but haven't gone much father than just lookin' and thinkin'<P>Terry K said something about there being diffrent mounts or something so it's not just a bolt-in BUT I'd Like to try it. <P>Brian <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||WKDFIRO||03-18-2001||05:22 PM||||Could you buy one new with this engine in 88?-Yes <P>You mean unbeknownst to EVERYONE that 88 Fieros had a turbo 2.0 option? Was it a double-secret option? (Animal House) lol<P>They were talking about it--Yes<P>3 prototypes using turbo 1.8s were built as a possible alternative to the V6 by Jay Wetzel of Pontiac Engineering. They ran 150 hp and rev'd up to 6800 rpms. It was decided against because the turbo would have been the GT and the non-turbo would have been the coupe. The non-turbo was even weaker than the 2.5. Also the Brazil engine plant couldn't produce engines for both the Sunbird and the Fiero.<P>In 88 two Alcan (ALL aluminum chassis!)prototypes were fitted with the Quad 4 putting out 190 hp!<P>Apparently only one of the prototypes turbos exist in the unofficial Pontiac museum of special Fieros.<P>Source: Fiero by Gary Witzenburg (LOVE this book!)<P>Personally, I wouldn't want to sacrifice the low end torque going to a 2.0. Even the 2.5 has more torque than even some of today's imports! But some people just HAVE to be different!<P>I would love to see the article if you still have it Brian!<P> <p>[This message has been edited by WKDFIRO (edited 03-18-2001).]||||reg||4
